## Ranked Findings

### Finding 1 (Severity: Low / Precision) — Dual Claim Attribution in Lede
* **Location:** [`chapters/04-spray-crew-file.html:25`](file:///home/diablo/book19/chapters/04-spray-crew-file.html#L25) (Lede)
* **Quoted Passage:**  
  > *"The Dutch exposure limits changed in April 2026, while the crew's training records have already been mandatory for three years. `<!-- CHECK: 04-limits -->` `<!-- CHECK: 04-reach-duty -->`"*
* **Source Reality:**  
  [`04-limits.txt`](file:///home/diablo/book19/resources/sources/04/excerpts/04-limits.txt) verifies the April 2026 exposure limits change under Staatsblad 2025-337, whereas [`04-reach-duty.txt`](file:///home/diablo/book19/resources/sources/04/excerpts/04-reach-duty.txt) verifies the 24 August 2023 REACH Annex XVII training mandate. Placing both markers at the end of the compound sentence clusters two distinct receipts.
* **Concrete Fix:**  
  Position each marker directly after its corresponding clause:  
  *"The Dutch exposure limits changed in April 2026 `<!-- CHECK: 04-limits -->`, while the crew's training records have already been mandatory for three years `<!-- CHECK: 04-reach-duty -->`."*

---

### Finding 2 (Severity: Low / Clarity) — Separation of Founder Replacement Labour and Owner Surplus
* **Location:** [`chapters/04-spray-crew-file.html:77`](file:///home/diablo/book19/chapters/04-spray-crew-file.html#L77) (Section 5: Economics)
* **Quoted Passage:**  
  > *"Founder replacement is owner compensation, not free labour. The €30,000 remainder is company surplus and must absorb claims, idle days and hiring variance."*
* **Source Reality & Rule Context:**  
  Under [AGENT.md Priority 3](file:///home/diablo/book19/AGENT.md#L20), founder replacement cost (the market rate to hire an operational replacement) and owner return/surplus (the equity profit) must remain distinct. Stating *"Founder replacement is owner compensation"* risks confusing operational labour expense with equity dividend.
* **Concrete Fix:**  
  Clarify the prose:  
  *"Founder replacement is the market cost of replacing operational and sales labour, not free effort. The €30,000 remainder is owner surplus and company buffer, which must absorb claims, idle days and hiring variance."*

---

### Finding 3 (Severity: Low / Polish) — Explicit Label for Comparator Hourly Rate in Section 5
* **Location:** [`chapters/04-spray-crew-file.html:68`](file:///home/diablo/book19/chapters/04-spray-crew-file.html#L68) (Section 5: Economics)
* **Quoted Passage:**  
  > *"Every price is a labelled design hurdle except ArboNed's checked €192-per-hour public comparator. `<!-- CHECK: 04-arboned-price -->`"*
* **Source Reality:**  
  [`04-arboned-price.txt`](file:///home/diablo/book19/resources/sources/04/excerpts/04-arboned-price.txt) quotes blocks of 2h (€384), 4h (€768), and 8h (€1,536). €384 / 2 = €192/h. While the arithmetic is exact, the source text itself specifies block packages.
* **Concrete Fix:**  
  Clarify the derivation in the sentence:  
  *"Every price is a labelled design hurdle except ArboNed's checked €192-per-hour public comparator (derived from its €384 two-hour block). `<!-- CHECK: 04-arboned-price -->`"*

